{%- comment -%}
The swept scorecard, republished at a stable URL.

_data/ is Jekyll's and never reaches the built site, so anything that wants this
data — the MCP server, a bump bot, a spreadsheet — needs it served from
somewhere. Serving it from the same build that renders the board means the two
can never disagree about what the fleet looks like.

Findings detail is not inlined. It sits beside this file under findings/, one
file per repository, which is what the board fetches on demand.
